Third-party components:

  Vendored Rust crates under /vendor are redistributed under their own
  OSI-approved / permissive licences; the release gate enforces an allow-list
  (`just check-licences`). Each retains its own copyright and licence, listed in
  the generated CycloneDX SBOM (`*.sbom.cdx.json`).

  The consoles and the design documentation bundle three typefaces, each
  licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 (OFL-1.1):
  Oxanium (Copyright 2019 The Oxanium Project Authors), Space Grotesk
  (Copyright 2020 The Space Grotesk Project Authors) and JetBrains Mono
  (Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors). The font files and their
  licence texts are in ui/design-system/src/fonts and docs/design/fonts.

  The Heimdall console's 3D globe bundles three.js (Copyright 2010-2026 three.js
  authors), licensed under the MIT License, and outlines from Natural Earth
  (naturalearthdata.com, version 5.1.2), which is in the public domain: coastlines,
  land polygons and land borders at 1:110m and 1:50m, in
  products/heimdall/ui/src/globe/data, built by tools/heimdall-outlines/build.mjs.
  Made with Natural Earth.

  The Heimdall console's 2D geographic map decodes vector tiles with
  @mapbox/vector-tile and pbf (Copyright Mapbox, BSD-3-Clause), which bring
  @mapbox/point-geometry (Copyright Mapbox, ISC), resolve-protobuf-schema and
  protocol-buffers-schema (Copyright Mathias Buus, MIT). The built console ships
  the licence texts of what it bundles in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md.
  resolve-protobuf-schema and protocol-buffers-schema serve only pbf's schema
  compiler (its CLI): they are in the dependency closure and the SBOM, but no
  console bundle includes them.

  With its map tiles switch on (VITE_HEIMDALL_TILES, the default), the Heimdall
  console fetches map tiles at run time from three sources. None of their data is
  bundled; the tests use three recorded tiles, credited in
  products/heimdall/ui/fixtures/tiles/CREDITS.md. The console's CREDITS control
  shows each source while it is in use.

